<Project>
  <!--
    The Cleat C# SDK, imported by a workflow project (cleat#4080). It is a SOURCE package: the SDK's types sit
    on top of bindings that the componentize toolchain generates INSIDE the consuming project, so they cannot be
    precompiled. This file adds the SDK's sources to the project and points the component toolchain at the one
    WIT world the engine reads.

    The project properties the toolchain needs (target framework, runtime identifier, trimming, the pinned
    package references) are the build chain's, not this file's: see the fixture's .csproj, and PR 2 of cleat#4080
    for the template that the csharp target of `cleat build` generates.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <CleatSdkDir>$([MSBuild]::EnsureTrailingSlash('$([System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..'))'))</CleatSdkDir>
    <!-- Inside a repo checkout the world is python-sdk/wit/cleat.wit, the file the engine's tests read. A packed
         SDK carries a byte-identical copy at wit/cleat.wit (a test compares them). -->
    <CleatWitFile Condition="'$(CleatWitFile)' == '' and Exists('$(CleatSdkDir)wit/cleat.wit')">$(CleatSdkDir)wit/cleat.wit</CleatWitFile>
    <CleatWitFile Condition="'$(CleatWitFile)' == ''">$([System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath('$(CleatSdkDir)../../python-sdk/wit/cleat.wit'))</CleatWitFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    THE GC SEGMENT SIZE: ONE CONSTANT, AND IT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS BLOCK (cleat#4378).

    A NativeAOT-LLVM guest on WASI starts a workstation GC with three 16 MiB heap segments (small-object, large-object, pinned: the 32-bit
    defaults, INITIAL_ALLOC and LHEAP_ALLOC in the runtime's gc.cpp), and the WASI layer's VirtualReserve is posix_memalign followed by
    memset(0) (gc/wasm/gcenv.wasm.cpp), so "reserving" a segment WRITES all of it. An empty workflow therefore cost 48.7 MiB of private
    memory per instance (measured as a fit over N = 1 to 64 instances, R2 = 1.0000), before it had allocated a byte.

    GCSegmentSize is the GC's own setting for that size, and 4 MiB is its floor (anything smaller is raised to 4 MiB). At 8 MiB, the value
    chosen here, an empty workflow costs 16.7 MiB per instance and starts in 296 pages of linear memory instead of 809 (same fit, same
    machine). At the 4 MiB floor it costs 12.7 MiB and starts in 232 pages, and the trade-off below is the same size, so the choice of 8 is
    the owner's (2026-11-22) and not a measurement's.

    IT IS A PRIVATE GC SETTING, so it must be embedded with the ILCompiler's runtimeopt switch, which is how it passes ServerGarbageCollection.
    A RuntimeHostConfigurationOption becomes the runtimeknob switch and carries PUBLIC keys only: GCSegmentSize set that way is read back by
    managed code as a switch and does nothing. DOTNET_GCSegmentSize in the environment did nothing either, in every form tried.
    (No double hyphen may appear in this comment: XML forbids it, and the build then fails to evaluate this file at all.)

    THE TRADE-OFF, measured: a workflow that holds many large (large-object-heap) objects pays about 26% over its data, from segment rounding
    (16 MiB held in 1 MiB arrays moved the per-instance cost by 20.5 MiB at 8 MiB segments, against 16.2 MiB with the default segments).
    Large allocations still work: 16, 64 and 128 MiB of 1 MiB arrays completed. Set CleatGcSegmentSizeHex in the project to choose another
    value, and tests/csharp pins the start-up memory and the per-instance cost this default gives.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <CleatGcSegmentSizeHex Condition="'$(CleatGcSegmentSizeHex)' == ''">0x800000</CleatGcSegmentSizeHex>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <IlcArg Include="--runtimeopt:GCSegmentSize=$(CleatGcSegmentSizeHex)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(CleatSdkDir)src/**/*.cs" Visible="false" />
    <Wit Include="$(CleatWitFile)" World="cleat-workflow" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
